KW  - CPFEM
KW  - Fracture mechanics
KW  - Dynamic Bayesian network
KW  - CYCLIC PLASTICITY
KW  - IRON
AB  - Fatigue cracks are prone to initiate in rib-to-deck (RTD) weld joints of orthotropic steel decks (OSD) under traffic loading, posing a serious threat to functionality and safety of bridge structures. To achieve accurate fatigue crack life prediction of RTD weld joints of OSD, a digital twin-based multiscale fatigue crack life prediction framework from microcrack initiation and propagation to macrocrack propagation is proposed. Eccentric tensile fatigue tests as a physical entity are first conducted to obtain test data on fatigue crack propagation. A multiscale crack propagation model coupling crystal plasticity finite element model with fracture mechanics is then established as a virtual entity to describe microcrack initiation and propagation as well as macrocrack propagation. A dynamic Bayesian network integrated with a particle filter algorithm is finally introduced to fuse the test data from the physical entity with the numerical results from the virtual entity, enabling real-time updating of key model parameters and crack propagation states as well as quantitative uncertainty assessment and digital twin construction. The results from this study demonstrate that the proposed digital twin effectively suppresses model uncertainty and significantly improves the prediction accuracy of crack propagation process and remaining fatigue life.
