AB  - Traditional electrical resistivity tomography (ERT) inversion for dam leakage detection faces heavy computational loads and smoothness priors that fail to localize anomalies. This study introduces the Topology-Guided Fourier Neural Operator framework. A Fourier Neural Operator replaces the numerical solver based on the governing equations, speeding up forward potential field simulations. To easily locate anomalies, a decoupled geometric parameterization separates the deterministic defect from the stochastic background. A Navigator network extracts coarse topological priors to initialize a parallel multi-hypothesis workflow. Tested across multiple trials, the framework achieves a 99.7% average success rate and an 89.3% high-fidelity reconstruction rate. It accelerates forward modeling by 345 times and overall inversion by 72 times compared to finite element methods. The method detects unseen low-contrast early leakages and remains stable under 20% measurement noise and 50% data loss. This approach provides the efficiency and reliability requisite for routine safety monitoring and operational digital twins.
