TI  - Real-time multivariate forecasting of rail temperature with TimeGPT-1
T2  - JOURNAL OF CIVIL STRUCTURAL HEALTH MONITORING
LA  - English
KW  - Meteorological data
KW  - Rail temperature prediction
KW  - Real-time forecasting
KW  - TimeGPT-1
KW  - Time-series prediction
AB  - Thermal buckling of railway tracks is a critical safety concern during hot weather and is expected to become more severe under a warming climate. Reliable rail-temperature forecasting is therefore essential for proactive railway operation. However, existing forecasting approaches are often limited by short prediction horizons, insufficient accuracy, or dependence on inputs unavailable for real-time operation. To address these limitations, this study proposes a foundation-model-based rail-temperature forecasting framework using TimeGPT-1, a pretrained time-series foundation model adapted through lightweight fine-tuning. The model uses routinely available meteorological variables, including air temperature, solar radiation, sunshine duration, relative humidity, wind speed, and rainfall, to predict rail temperature up to six hours ahead. Meteorological observations from the Seoul Weather Station and rail-temperature measurements from Dongjak Station collected between July 2015 and September 2017 were used for model development and evaluation. Under leakage-free rolling-origin validation, the proposed model achieved a mean absolute error (MAE) of 1.33 degrees C and a root mean squared error (RMSE) of 1.58 degrees C, while maintaining stable accuracy across all forecasting horizons. A controlled benchmarking study showed that the proposed framework outperformed conventional statistical, recurrent, transformer-based, and Chronos-2 foundation models under an identical evaluation protocol. Aggregated SHAP analysis identified air temperature and solar radiation as the dominant predictors under normal conditions, whereas rainfall became more influential during heavy-rainfall periods, consistent with heat-transfer mechanisms. The proposed framework provides an accurate, interpretable, and practical solution for real-time rail-temperature forecasting and supports digital twin-enabled railway infrastructure management through early warning of thermal buckling risk.
